# ── measurement corpora: ignored, and regenerable by measuring again ──
# 2.7 GB of frames, runs and logs. They used to live in `docs`, which is why
# that word meant "2.7 GB of captures plus five markdown files" and why the
# five had no history worth speaking of. The name now says what it is, and it
# sits under the layer that PRODUCES it.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS A WHITELISTED PATH, NOT A LICENCE FOR calibration/. The rule
# calibration/CLAUDE.md states -- "artifacts go under docs/, not next to the
# source; a script that regresses to writing beside the code makes git status
# dirty, and that is the mechanism that finds it" -- still holds, and this is
# now its ONE legal sink. Anything else a script writes into calibration/
# still shows up dirty, which is the whole point.
calibration/artifacts

# ── what a clean clone must RUN with, therefore versioned ──
# data/ is the counterpart: everything the runtime or a gate LOADS. Curves
# (with no curve the tool does not compensate), detector templates (with no
# templates a fresh checkout has no lobby chain, no weapon-name OCR and no
# posture), the measured scale tables, and the two gate baselines.
#
# ⚠ THE GLOBAL *.png / *.jpg / *.npz RULES ABOVE MATCH AT EVERY DEPTH, so the
# templates need explicit re-inclusion or they vanish from a clone while
# `git status` stays clean. That failure has already happened once in this
# repo, to the curves: docs/ was ignored wholesale, a cleanup deleted
# docs/recoil/curves/, and 40 weapons' curves went with it with nothing to
# revert to. Re-includes are per-rule, not per-tree.
!data/
!data/**/
!data/**/*.png
!data/**/*.jpg
!data/**/*.npz
!data/**/*.json
!data/**/*.jsonl
!data/**/*.md

# (data/templates/highlight_eval/ is 15 MB of labelled eval corpus and is NOT
#  a template the runtime loads -- it is a corpus, so by the rule above it
#  belongs in calibration/artifacts/. Left where it is for now; moving it is a
#  separate change and it is small enough not to force one today.)
#
# ⚠ weapon_hud_bank.npz IS TRACKED, 2.8 MB, and it took a decision to get
# there. It is DERIVED -- calibration/build_weapon_hud_bank.py builds it --
# but its corpus (Manual/weapon_hud, 128 MB) was deleted on 2026-08-08, so
# "just rebuild it" stopped being true and it became an unrebuildable ignored
# file, which is the worst of both. detector/weapon_hud_detector.py loads it
# at import, so a clone without it has no weapon-HUD identification at all.
#
# .githooks/pre-commit refuses NEW files over 2 MB, on size rather than on any
# argument about what a file means, precisely so that this cannot happen by
# drift. Getting it in took `--no-verify` and an explicit human decision --
# which is the hook working as designed, not being worked around.

# (highlight_eval/ and weapon_hud_bank.npz stay OUT: 15 MB of labelled eval
#  corpus and a 2.9 MB PCA bank. The bank is derived — but ⚠ as of 2026-08-08
#  its corpus (Manual/weapon_hud, 128 MB) is DELETED, so "rebuild it with
#  calibration/build_weapon_hud_bank.py" is no longer true. It is now an
#  unrebuildable ignored file, which is the worst of both; if that matters,
#  the fix is to track it, not to pretend the corpus is coming back.)


